[
    {
        "content": "<p>I thought it would be cute (unsure how practical) to define an <code>HMul</code> instance on some props. For instance there's <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/Asymptotics/Defs.html#Asymptotics.IsBigO.mul\">Asymptotics.IsBigO.mul</a> and so I thought I could write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_13</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_17</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SeminormedRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormMulClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>what I thought would be really nice is how this can overload, for instance there's also <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/Asymptotics/Defs.html#Asymptotics.IsBigO.mul_isLittleO\">Asymptotics.IsBigO.mul_isLittleO</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/Asymptotics/Defs.html#Asymptotics.IsLittleO.mul_isBigO\">Asymptotics.IsLittleO.mul_isBigO</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/Asymptotics/Defs.html#Asymptotics.IsBigO.const_mul_left\">Asymptotics.IsBigO.const_mul_left</a> and these could all get a nice short <code>ha * hb</code> notation instead of remembering the different name for each separate theorem of the form \"construct a bound on a product\".</p>\n<p>Sadly <code>HMul</code> only takes <code>Type _</code> instead of <code>Sort</code>s, and so the best you can do is write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PLift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PLift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PLift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Asymptotics</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsBigO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">down</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">down</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but then you get ugly usage like <code>(PLift.up ha * PLift.up hb).down</code>, which is certainly worse than <code>ha.mul hb</code>.</p>\n<p>Or I could write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- `a * b` computes the product of `a` and `b`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  The meaning of this notation is type-dependent. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inherit_doc</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">infixl</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">69</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" ⋆ \"</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but I have to give it some funny symbol like <code>⋆</code> instead of <code>*</code> because otherwise conventional multiplication breaks. :( </p>\n<p>Anyway, is there a particular reason that notations like HMul <em>don't</em> support Prop?</p>",
        "id": 599570180,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1780420827
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"448405\">Alex Meiburg</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599570180\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>but I have to give it some funny symbol like <code>⋆</code> instead of <code>*</code> because otherwise conventional multiplication breaks. :(</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Do you have an example of this?</p>",
        "id": 599570518,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780420922
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, here's one from the file I was working on:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_13</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_17</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SeminormedRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormMulClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- `a * b` computes the product of `a` and `b`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  The meaning of this notation is type-dependent. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">--precedence 71 matches the existing notation</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inherit_doc</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">infixl</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">71</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" * \"</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"n\">O</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atTop</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atBot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It gives</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Ambiguous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Possible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">interpretations</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">15</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">18</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">9</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599571215,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1780421135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think a nice answer here would be to allow writing <code>congr($h1 * $h2)</code> for this BigO case</p>",
        "id": 599572511,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780421469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(or perhaps <code>gcongr( )</code>)</p>",
        "id": 599572533,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780421478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the channel is private, but there was some work done at the recent ICERM workshop on an elaborator/delaborator for big O notation that is probably what is ultimately wanted</p>",
        "id": 599576072,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780422381
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think that's what Alex wants - I think he wants something where a proof can look like <code>ha * hb</code>, whereas that discussion makes it cleaner to state things in big O (not prove them)</p>",
        "id": 599577359,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1780422692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I see. I guess this could be more widely useful too, like connectives in logics?</p>",
        "id": 599582969,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780423970
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd hope so! I'm sure some people wouldn't like this (these notations should be used for data and using them for proofs could be too confusing ... or something) but I think it could also look very elegant.</p>",
        "id": 599586694,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1780425021
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that linear_combination allows the (very nice) <code>2 * ha + 3 * hb</code> syntax to mean \"double the inequality ha and triple the inequality hb and add them together\", so there's precedent for using operations on propositions. This particular approach does it as part of a tactic's syntax, so it would require duplication but also not clash with things like you saw in your example.</p>",
        "id": 599587264,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1780425177
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think congr() has to be taught about new syntax in the way that <code>linear_combination</code> does</p>",
        "id": 599587800,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780425337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think a <code>gcongr(...)</code> elaborator would make sense. It would take some effort to implement it though. It would need to use <code>@[gcongr]</code> lemmas in a forwards reasoning way, instead of backwards reasoning (which is how they are currently used).</p>",
        "id": 599594971,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780427339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>9 messages were moved from this topic to <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"270676\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/PSigma.20and.20universe.20levels/with/599849707\">#lean4 &gt; PSigma and universe levels</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"111080\">Floris van Doorn</span>.</p>",
